TOUCHSTONE OVERVIEW
==================

1. Introduction
---------------

Touchstone is a benchmarking platform used to evaluate the performance, functionality, scalability, stability, and reliability of cloud environments. It allows users to create environments, organize test suites, execute benchmark tests, monitor executions, and analyze results through reports and graphs.

The typical Touchstone workflow is:

1. Create an Environment.
2. Create a Test Suite.
3. Add Test Cases.
4. Configure execution parameters.
5. Execute the Test Suite.
6. Monitor the execution.
7. Review reports and graphs.
8. Compare results with reference benchmarks.


====================================================================
2. Environments
====================================================================

An Environment represents the cloud platform where benchmark tests are executed.

Touchstone supports two environment types:

• Kubernetes
• OpenStack


2.1 Kubernetes
--------------

Kubernetes is a container orchestration platform used to deploy and manage containerized workloads.

Touchstone supports both private and public Kubernetes clusters.

Private Kubernetes Clusters

• SR-IOV
  - Intel NIC-based cluster

• OCP (OpenShift Container Platform)
  - Mellanox (MLNX) NIC-based cluster

• Multimaster
  - Multiple master node configuration

Public Kubernetes Clusters

• Google Kubernetes Engine (GKE)
• Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS)
• Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)

Note:
Public cloud environments require billing to be enabled before they can be used.


2.2 OpenStack
-------------

OpenStack is an Infrastructure-as-a-Service (IaaS) platform used to provision virtual machines.

Supported OpenStack releases:

• Zed
• Bobcat

OpenStack also serves as the underlying infrastructure for creating internal Kubernetes clusters.


