4. Test Suites and Test Cases
====================================================================

4.1 Test Suites
---------------

A Test Suite is a collection of related Test Cases grouped by a testing area.

When a new Touchstone VM is created, it contains only the system-defined Test Suites for that release.

Users typically create their own Test Suites by selecting the required Test Cases.

Industry benchmark Test Suites are also available as reference baselines for performance comparison.


4.2 Test Cases
--------------

A Test Case represents a specific benchmark scenario executed against an environment.

Each Test Case consists of:

• Scenario
• Tool
• Context


Scenarios
---------

Examples include:

• Throughput
• Latency
• Network Latency
• Packet Loss

Most Test Cases support both IPv4 and IPv6.


Tools
-----

Each benchmarking tool has a unique identifier.

Examples:

Tool ID    Tool
-------    ----------------
1          iperf
2          pktgen
11         pro
21         trafgen


Context
-------

Context defines how a Test Case is executed.

Examples:

• KG - Different nodes
• KA - Same node

Contexts are classified into two categories.

Existing Context

• Resources are created before execution.
• Execution uses those existing resources.
• Test Cases are identified with an additional "X".
• Resource definitions are provided through YAML files.

Non-Existing Context

• Touchstone automatically creates the required resources.
• Kubernetes uses a server image.
• OpenStack uses a QCOW2 image.

These images contain all required benchmarking tools.


