6. Test Execution
====================================================================

A Test Suite is executed on a selected Environment with the required execution parameters.

Each execution follows these stages:

1. Initialization
2. Context Creation
3. Benchmark Execution
4. Result Collection
5. Cleanup

Execution history is maintained on the Execution page.


====================================================================
7. Benchmark Images
====================================================================

Different environment types require different execution images.

Kubernetes

• A Docker image containing the latest benchmark code is used to execute Kubernetes NFVI Test Cases.

OpenStack

• A QCOW2 image containing the latest benchmark code is used to execute OpenStack NFVI Test Cases.

Bare Metal

Bare metal execution requires a Host SSH Proxy.

The Host SSH Proxy contains:

• Whitelist of permitted commands
• Blacklist of restricted commands

This controls which commands Touchstone is allowed to execute on the host.


====================================================================
8. Reports
====================================================================

After execution completes, Touchstone generates execution reports.

Reports include:

• Benchmark results
• Reference comparison
• Performance metrics
• Graphical visualization of benchmark results

Reports are linked to each execution and can be viewed from the Execution page.


====================================================================
9. Monitoring
====================================================================

Touchstone provides monitoring during execution at both:

• Node level
• Container level

Monitoring is visualized using Grafana dashboards.

Common metrics include:

• CPU utilization
• Memory utilization


